# Legacy Audit

Purpose:
  One-time transition procedure for pre-existing (vibe-coded) code before CASE spec creation.
  Reviews existing code against the 5-step skill chain and records findings as tasks.

Owns: legacy\AUDIT-README.sdd

## Procedure

Trigger:
  When a new .sdd spec is created for an existing BE/FE/MD directory.

Steps:
  1. Read real code in the target directory.
  2. Review against the 5-step skill chain (FEATURE → FIX → BUG → SECURITY-REVIEW → ULTRA-REVIEW) in review mode.
  3. IF no findings:
       - CASE Tasks list starts fully marked [x].
  4. IF findings exist:
       - Add each finding as [ ] in the CASE Tasks list.
       - Annotate continuation line with: `origin: legacy-audit`

## Task Annotation Format

Tasks:
  [ ] #1 {finding description}
      origin: legacy-audit, attempt_count: 0/3

## Lifecycle

Legacy_Status: pending|in_progress|completed
Audit_Date: <timestamp>
Auditor: <agent or human>

State: +
